{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01255",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.72,
      "end_seconds": 8.21,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Okay, so doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.04,
      "end_seconds": 15.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Right, not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 16.31,
      "end_seconds": 23.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "Um, um, good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.53,
      "end_seconds": 37.92,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a sore ankle. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.05,
      "end_seconds": 47.34,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.05,
      "end_seconds": 57.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.48,
      "text": "I'd call it severe. Yes, walking. That makes it worse. Honestly, a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.46,
      "end_seconds": 66.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 67.04,
      "end_seconds": 73.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, um, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.14,
      "end_seconds": 77.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "I, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.78,
      "end_seconds": 83.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Have you had a sore ankle before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.35,
      "end_seconds": 89.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "A bit, last winter. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 95.18,
      "end_seconds": 97.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.64,
      "end_seconds": 115.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Did you get numbness, pain in the foot or crack or pop?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.81,
      "end_seconds": 134.84,
      "duration_seconds": 18.03,
      "text": "Um, no, no numbness, no pain in the foot, no crack or pop. I did have a little swelling at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.55,
      "end_seconds": 139.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.37,
      "end_seconds": 142.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.64,
      "end_seconds": 148.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.11,
      "end_seconds": 151.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.42,
      "end_seconds": 155.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Okay, a few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.32,
      "end_seconds": 168.26,
      "duration_seconds": 10.94,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. I gave up cigarettes last spring. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.99,
      "end_seconds": 175.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.75,
      "end_seconds": 183.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "I'm on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day. Mirtazapine, 15 milligrams, maybe, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.46,
      "end_seconds": 188.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.01,
      "end_seconds": 192.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "No, it's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.56,
      "end_seconds": 203.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "It's, It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.19,
      "end_seconds": 207.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.72,
      "end_seconds": 220.57,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "I mean, for my migraines, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.97,
      "end_seconds": 226.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.66,
      "end_seconds": 232.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "My father had bowel cancer. My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.23,
      "end_seconds": 236.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.04,
      "end_seconds": 240.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "I've had heart disease, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.72,
      "end_seconds": 244.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Right, is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.71,
      "end_seconds": 252.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "Depression, for about ten years. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.52,
      "end_seconds": 255.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.13,
      "end_seconds": 258.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Migraines, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.26,
      "end_seconds": 263.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Alright, migraines, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.25,
      "end_seconds": 285.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.26,
      "end_seconds": 296.32,
      "duration_seconds": 10.06,
      "text": "Yes, milk. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.21,
      "end_seconds": 300.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.31,
      "end_seconds": 306.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Just an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.52,
      "end_seconds": 310.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.48,
      "end_seconds": 324.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.96,
      "end_seconds": 345.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.41,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 74 beats a minute, height 179 centimetres, weight 86 kilos. And blood pressure 116 over 80, temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.09,
      "end_seconds": 351.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.24,
      "end_seconds": 355.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Alright, breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.18,
      "end_seconds": 375.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "There's mild swelling over the outside of the ankle, and you can put your weight on it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.3,
      "end_seconds": 389.84,
      "duration_seconds": 11.54,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Having listened and examined, I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at a mild ankle sprain or a minor fracture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 390.78,
      "end_seconds": 394.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.01,
      "end_seconds": 411.0,
      "duration_seconds": 14.99,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a mild ankle sprain, and we'll watch how it goes. So, to recap quickly. You've had a sore ankle, severe, and no crack or pop or numbness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.01,
      "end_seconds": 413.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.68,
      "end_seconds": 438.37,
      "duration_seconds": 23.69,
      "text": "Rest, ice, a compression bandage and keep it raised for two days. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Let's plan a check if it is not better in two weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.07,
      "end_seconds": 442.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}